#
# holt — Terraform for a ctags that has no Terraform parser.
#
# Loaded ONLY when holt has measured that this toolchain cannot extract Terraform symbols.
# universal-ctags gained a Terraform parser in 6.x; Ubuntu 24.04 LTS ships 5.9.0, so on the
# most common Linux install holt would otherwise report "no symbols" for every .tf file and,
# because silence reads as "nothing there", quietly claim two agents editing the same
# infrastructure had nothing in common.
#
# The language is defined under a PRIVATE NAME. `--langdef=Terraform` on a ctags that already has
# a Terraform parser is not a warning — it is FATAL, exit 1, and the entire ctags run dies, so a
# single misjudged probe would take symbol extraction down for every modern user. A private name
# cannot collide with a builtin, which makes this pack safe to load even when it is not needed.
# holt still only loads it after MEASURING the gap, so a working builtin parser is never replaced
# by these regexes; the private name is the second line of defence, not the first.
#
--langdef=HoltTerraform
--map-HoltTerraform=+.tf
--map-HoltTerraform=+.tfvars
--kinddef-HoltTerraform=r,resource,resources
--kinddef-HoltTerraform=d,data,data sources
--kinddef-HoltTerraform=v,variable,variables
--kinddef-HoltTerraform=o,output,outputs
--kinddef-HoltTerraform=m,module,modules
--kinddef-HoltTerraform=p,provider,providers
--regex-HoltTerraform=/^[ \t]*resource[ \t]+"[^"]+"[ \t]+"([^"]+)"/\1/r/
--regex-HoltTerraform=/^[ \t]*data[ \t]+"[^"]+"[ \t]+"([^"]+)"/\1/d/
--regex-HoltTerraform=/^[ \t]*variable[ \t]+"([^"]+)"/\1/v/
--regex-HoltTerraform=/^[ \t]*output[ \t]+"([^"]+)"/\1/o/
--regex-HoltTerraform=/^[ \t]*module[ \t]+"([^"]+)"/\1/m/
--regex-HoltTerraform=/^[ \t]*provider[ \t]+"([^"]+)"/\1/p/
